 "sheet": [
  "Open news with the fact, not the weather: who did what, where, when, in the first sentence, in the active voice. Typical Kommersant lede: subject, predicate, number, then one clause of context.",
  "Put the freshest or most consequential detail first; the \"why it matters\" belongs in the second or third sentence and must be a concrete consequence (cost, deadline, who is affected), never the phrase \"это важно\".",
  "Vary sentence length on purpose: a 25-word sentence with a subordinate clause, then a 6-word one. Never run three sentences of the same length or the same first word in a row.",
  "Prefer finite verbs to verbal nouns. Write \"власти повысили сбор\", not \"было осуществлено повышение сборов\". Cut -ение/-ание/-ация chains; one verbal noun per sentence at most.",
  "Break chains of genitives: no more than two nouns in the genitive in a row. \"Уровень качества обслуживания клиентов\" becomes \"насколько хорошо обслуживают клиентов\".",
  "Limit participial and adverbial-participle (деепричастный) clauses to one per sentence, and never close a sentence with a decorative gerund (\"…, подчёркивая важность…\"). If the clause carries a fact, make it a separate sentence with its own verb.",
  "Use the passive and \"является\" sparingly. Replace \"является\" with the dash only where grammar demands it (subject-predicate between nouns: \"Лимассол — крупнейший порт острова\") or with a real verb.",
  "Use the dash (тире) only for grammatical cases: between subject and predicate nouns, apposition, a sharp break, direct speech. Do not use it as a substitute for commas or a colon, and never more than a few times per page.",
  "Verb aspect: use perfective for completed news events (\"правительство утвердило\"), imperfective for processes and background (\"рынок растёт\"). Mixing them carelessly is a translation tell.",
  "Rotate attribution verbs: сказал, пояснил, признал, добавил, заметил, напомнил, уточнил, отметил, возразил, настаивает, считает. Use \"подчеркнул\" at most once per piece. Prefer plain \"сказал\" after a long quote.",
  "Attribute to named sources with role and date: \"заместитель министра финансов Мариос Христу заявил в понедельник…\". Ban \"эксперты считают\", \"по мнению аналитиков\" unless followed by a name or a document.",
  "Quote with guillemets «…». Nested quotes use „…“ inside («…„…“…»). Direct speech layout: «Текст», — сказал он. Dash and capital rules apply: «Текст, — сказал он, — продолжение».",
  "Numbers: thousands separated by a non-breaking space (1 200 000), decimals with a comma (3,5 %), the percent sign after a non-breaking space, the euro sign after the amount (1 200 €) or the word \"евро\". Never \"1,200\", \"€1 200\", \"3.5%\".",
  "Dates: \"5 октября 2026 года\", in a sentence-middle \"5 октября 2026 года\" stays complete; \"в 2026 году\", \"с 1 января\". No \"October 5, 2026\", no \"05.10.2026\" in running prose. Weekdays in lower case.",
  "Headings in Russian are sentence case: only the first word and proper names are capitalised. \"Как получить вид на жительство на Кипре\", never \"Как Получить Вид На Жительство На Кипре\". No full stop at the end; no ALL-CAPS.",
  "Use ё consistently or not at all; for a magazine of this level either is acceptable, but do not mix within a piece. Check \"всё\" (pronoun) against \"все\".",
  "Cut connectors by default. A paragraph needs \"кроме того\", \"более того\", \"также\", \"однако\", \"тем не менее\" only when the logic truly turns; a second connector in the same paragraph is a failure.",
  "Do not close a piece with a moral or a summary paragraph. End on the latest fact, a quote, an image or a date to watch: \"Решение ожидается до конца ноября.\"",
  "Avoid the \"не только… но и\" and \"это не просто… а…\" frames and the rhetorical contrast \"дело не в X, а в Y\"; state Y directly. Allow at most one per long piece.",
  "No triplets by reflex. If three items are real, give them as a plain list with numbers; if two matter, name two. Break the rhythm \"А, Б и В\" with a figure or a proper noun.",
  "Replace hype adjectives with a verifiable specific: not \"живописная деревня\", but \"двадцать домов из жёлтого камня над ущельем Диаррицос\". One sensory detail beats three adjectives.",
  "Kill English calques: \"в конце дня\", \"скрытая жемчужина\", \"сделать смысл\", \"брать место\", \"на регулярной основе\", \"в терминах\", \"играть роль\" in a business context, \"позиционировать себя как\", \"по-настоящему\", \"опыт\" meaning \"experience\".",
  "Use a native Russian press register: short verbs of action (запустили, отказали, вернули, обязали, купили), concrete nouns, minimal abstraction. Official words (осуществлять, обеспечивать, в рамках, данный) only when quoting a document.",
  "Real-estate and business pieces: give price per square metre, yield percentage, the tax rate, the statute or decree number, the date it takes effect. Replace \"высокий инвестиционный потенциал\" with the number and its source.",
  "Cyprus names: transliterate by the usual press practice (Лимасол, Никосия, Пафос, Ларнака, Айя-Напа, Протарас, Като-Пафос), keep Greek institutions in Russian with the original in brackets only at first mention (Министерство внутренних дел, Ypourgeio Esoterikon).",
  "Use the colon sparingly to introduce a quote, a definition or a list; do not turn every paragraph into \"Label: explanation\". Avoid markdown asterisks, hashes and emoji in body copy.",
  "Prefer simple tenses and the first-person plural only when the magazine acts (\"мы проверили\"). Avoid addressing the reader with \"вы узнаете\", \"давайте разберёмся\", \"представьте себе\" except in an interview or a column with a personal voice.",
  "Paragraphs of different length: one-sentence paragraphs are allowed for emphasis, but no more than one in four. No paragraph starts with the same word as the previous one.",
  "Use the unions \"а\", \"но\", \"зато\", \"впрочем\", \"правда\" to turn an argument naturally; the Russian colloquial \"зато\" and \"правда\" feel human where \"однако\" and \"тем не менее\" feel translated.",
  "Introduce a foreign term or an abbreviation once, with a short gloss: \"НДС (VAT)\", \"ТНВ (tax-resident non-dom)\". Prefer a Russian equivalent if the readers use it (\"вид на жительство\", not \"резидентство\").",
  "Opinion and review pieces may use a first-person voice and a clear verdict. Avoid \"стоит попробовать\", \"рекомендуем\", \"обязательно к посещению\"; give the dish, the price and the reason.",
  "Every paragraph must hold at least one detail that could not be written without reporting: a name, figure, place, date, quote, price, or a sensory observation. If it could be pasted into any other article, rewrite it."
 ],
